Chapter: RvFramelessImm

 A bitwise operation whose left side is a let-bound local and whose right
 side is a literal, in a function small enough to be emitted without a
 frame.

 On RISC-V this answered `bit-shl 8 8` -- 2048 -- where every other lane
 answers 42496, because the frameless path emitted the left operand into
 one of four rotating temporaries and then emitted the literal into a
 temporary the rotation handed back as the SAME register. The shift read
 its own amount as its value. `rv-alloc-temp` knows nothing about
 liveness, so nothing stopped it.

 Reduced from `j1939-encode`, which is where it was found: `j1939-pgn`
 recovers a PDU1 parameter group number as `bit-shl pf 8` over a let-bound
 `pf`, and answered 2277 instead of 65253. It only became reachable when
 the plug lanes started compiling optimised IR and
 `inline-leaf-calls` folded `j1939-pf` into its caller, which is what
 produced the let binding.

 **These are answers and not a shape on purpose.** The fix takes the
 I-type immediate form, so the register form is no longer emitted for
 these operands at all -- but a lane that lowers them some third way is
 equally welcome, provided it computes the same numbers.

 `and-big` is the guard, and it guards the bound the fix added: 4095 is
 above the 2047 an I-type immediate can hold, so the immediate path must
 decline it and the register form must run. An implementation that took
 it anyway would truncate the mask.

 **The shift bound is guarded in the emitter and deliberately NOT pinned
 here.** `rv-slli` masks an oversized shamt with #3F instead of refusing
 it, so the fix declines any shift amount above 63 -- but a shift that
 large already disagrees between the lanes for reasons that predate this
 work: `bit-shl x 2047` answers 0 on x86-64 and `x` shifted by 63 on
 RISC-V, because the hardware shift masks and x86's lowering does not.
 Pinning that here would put a permanent red row in the cross battery for
 a defect this test is not about, and it is open.

Section: Probe

  pf-of : Integer -> Integer
  pf-of (id) = bit-and (bit-shru id 16) 255

  shl-let : Integer -> Integer
  shl-let (id) =
   let pf = bit-and (bit-shru id 16) 255
   in bit-shl pf 8

  shl-let-if : Integer -> Integer
  shl-let-if (id) =
   let pf = bit-and (bit-shru id 16) 255
   in if pf < 240 then bit-shl pf 8
      else bit-or (bit-shl pf 8) (bit-and (bit-shru id 8) 255)

  shru-let : Integer -> Integer
  shru-let (id) =
   let pf = bit-and (bit-shru id 16) 65535
   in bit-shru pf 4

  and-let : Integer -> Integer
  and-let (id) =
   let pf = bit-shru id 16
   in bit-and pf 255

  or-let : Integer -> Integer
  or-let (id) =
   let pf = bit-and (bit-shru id 16) 255
   in bit-or pf 1024

  xor-let : Integer -> Integer
  xor-let (id) =
   let pf = bit-and (bit-shru id 16) 255
   in bit-xor pf 15

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (show (pf-of 419357952))
   print-line-uni (show (shl-let 419357952))
   print-line-uni (show (shl-let-if 419357952))
   print-line-uni (show (shl-let-if 111550464))
   print-line-uni (show (shru-let 419357952))
   print-line-uni (show (and-let 419357952))
   print-line-uni (show (or-let 419357952))
   print-line-uni (show (xor-let 419357952))
  end
